<!--Post: 73--><!--Time: 1085407825-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST73"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Doone<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Doone<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, May 24, 2004 - 7:10 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi.  Assuming BTK had been dormant between the 1970&#39;s murders until 1986 when he strangled Vicky Wegerle, what made him act out upon her?  I have been absorbed in this case and am hitting a saturation point, but there has been very little discussion of the Wegerle homocide on my favorite site, Kansas.com.  &#40;This site is moving up quickly,&#41;  From what we know Vicky had a husband, who was an apartment caretaker, one school age child and one 2 yr old toddler.  She had dropped the older child at school, and returned to her home on west 13th street.  Between 9am and the time her husband came home for lunch, she was strangled and placed in the bathtub.  Her toddler was found unharmed.  Mr Wegerle lived with being suspected for 18 yrs until the March photos and drivers license arrived in the mail.   <BR>What would activate a killer dormant for many years to target a young mother?  Did BTK live close to the Wegerles, work close by, obviously he had to be triggered in some aspect, because he didn&#39;t search the entire city for a young mom. <BR>Maybe this murder is the key to finding BTK.  It is the most recent that we know of and memories should be fresher.  Any ideas?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 73-->
<!--Post: 264--><!--Time: 1086972569-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST264"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jenkins<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jenkins<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, June 11, 2004 - 9:49 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->hmmmmmm.......... She had to trigger him some how indeed, to bring him out of dormancy. HOW HOW HOW HOW HOW HOW!!!!!!!!!!!!!???????????? <BR> <BR>hmmmmmmmmm......... <BR> <BR>I would expect something like that to take a bit of time perhaps regular interaction with her. Well I don&#39;t know, he didnt know her name, he showed the kid a picture and asked if the kid knew where this person lived. hmmm. So he didn&#39;t know a name, and didn&#39;t know where she lived. So it wasn&#39;t a peronal relationship. And he didnt live in the neighborhood because he didn&#39;t know where she lived. How did he get the pic? He had been stalking I&#39;m sure. Ok then. So why was he stalking her? <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 264-->
<!--Post: 265--><!--Time: 1086972717-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST265"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jenkins<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jenkins<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, June 11, 2004 - 9:51 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Oh, darn it, I was thinking of Vian! I think. It was vian whom he had to show a pic of someone and ask where this person lived. My bad. I just contributed absolutely nothing. I&#39;m sorry. LOL! <BR> <BR>again, hopefully after lunch I will regain coherency!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 265-->
<!--Post: 315--><!--Time: 1087934952-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST315"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Screamer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Screamer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, June 22, 2004 - 1:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yes, why did he wait so long to kill Wegerle? I myself have no idea. <BR> <BR>But, at the same time, why did he wait so long to take credit for this crime? I don&#39;t get it.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 315-->
<!--Post: 320--><!--Time: 1087954521-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST320"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, June 22, 2004 - 6:35 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi! <BR> <BR>Doone this is from some research I&#39;ve done. Could be coincidence perhaps. <BR> <BR>Vicky’s birthdate from her license looks like 3/25/58.  This is the feast of the Annunciation, when Mary conceived Jesus immaculately. Nancy Fox was killed on December 8th ,  the feast of the Immaculate Conception, a dogma which states Mary was born without sin &#40;immaculate&#41;. <BR><a href="http://www.wf-f.org/Annunciation.html" target=_top>http://www.wf-f.org/Annunciation.html</a> <BR> <BR>In 1858, 100 years before Vicky’s birthdate 1958, the Blessed Virgin appeared to  St. Bernadette on February 11. 2/11 or 211 is a number on Lindbergh’s Spirit of St. Louis when he crossed the Atlantic. The year 2004 is very close to Lindbergh’s birthdate of 2/04. Wichita was a stop on his &#40;TAT&#41; Transcontinental And Transport Line from New York to Los Angeles. <BR> <BR>St. Bernadette was born in 1844. Another victim, Nancy Fox was killed on 4/4 or 404 which is part of Vicky Wegerle’s address. <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.catholic-forum.com/saints/saintb06.htm" target=_top>http://www.catholic-forum.com/saints/saintb06.htm</a> <BR> <BR>Also you have similar address numbers, Otero 803, Nancy Fox 843, and the difference in numbers of the two 13th St. addresses, 3217 and 2404 is 813.  813 from 843 is 30. 2004 is 30 years since the first murders. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 320-->
<!--Post: 321--><!--Time: 1087961815-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST321"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, June 22, 2004 - 8:36 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Bookworm: don&#39;t ever change.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 321-->
<!--Post: 326--><!--Time: 1088086865-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST326"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, June 24, 2004 - 7:21 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks Ed, <BR> <BR>In Douglas&#39;s book Obsession he says BTK was complaining about the Otero&#39;s car being dirty. May be he liked cleanliness. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 326-->
<!--Post: 346--><!--Time: 1088266976-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST346"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, June 26, 2004 - 9:22 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here is more information that may correspond with the years of the murders and Vicky’s name, Wegerly and the name of the city Wichita. <BR> <BR>There is a map of the grotto of the Virgin apparitions, which is located near the end of a “wedge” of land v-shaped, formed by a small canal and the river Gave. <BR> <BR>In the book Bernadette also compares herself to a broom – she wished to be retired from the world “as an old broom is retired behind a door”.   Wichita sounds similar to witch, usually associated with brooms. <BR> <BR>The book that is my reference is Saint Bernadette Soubirous 1844-1879 by Abbe Francois Trochu, translated by John Joyce, S. J..  This book was first published in Paris, France in 1954, 20 years difference from 1974. 3 years later, 1977, &#40;also 20 years difference&#41; it was published in English in London. The current paperback version is copyrighted 1985 by Tan Books and Publishers, out of Rockford, Illinois. A year before Vicky was killed. Maybe BTK was familiar with this book. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 346-->
<!--Post: 360--><!--Time: 1088471927-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST360"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, June 28, 2004 - 6:18 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here is another possibility of why Vicky: the mural on the Kansas Aviation Museum, which can be seen on the first picture of it&#39;s website. The site says that the mural is made of natural colored rocks, but none could be found for the ocean part of the mural, so they crushed cobalt blue mentholatum jars and used them. &#34;Vicks&#34; is a mentolatum in that type jar. Sounds a lot like Vicky&#39;s or Vick&#39;s &#40;a nickname&#41; name. <BR> <BR>The only color that could not be found in stone was the dark cobalt blue of the ocean. That part of the panel was made from crushed Mentholatum jars.  <BR><a href="http://www.kansasaviationmuseum.org/aerodrome/building.html" target=_top>http://www.kansasaviationmuseum.org/aerodrome/buil ding.html</a> <BR> <BR>Also, Curly Locks is in Volume VI. The index of that set of books is Volume X. the poem was sent on an index card, a clue? Together VIX would sound like Vicks. <BR> <BR>Zodiac Connection <BR>“I will rub them down with deep heat to warm them up” From “Little List Letter” of July 26, 1970. This letter also speaks of buttons and torture. <BR><a href="http://www.zodiackiller.com/Mikado1.html" target=_top>http://www.zodiackiller.com/Mikado1.html</a> <BR> <BR>Maybe BTK is could also be trying to make a connection to the ocean or Lindbergh.  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 360-->
<!--Post: 594--><!--Time: 1090894180-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST594"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, July 26, 2004 - 7:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Another thing about BTK. If you look at the photos of his female victims, one thing becomes clear. You&#39;ll immediately see that none of them have a similar appearance. Julie Otero doesn&#39;t look like Vicky Wegerle, Shirley Vian does not resemble Nancy Fox, etc., etc. This <i>is</i> of some <BR>significance to a profiler, but I&#39;ve forgotten what. It&#39;s not rare, but it&#39;s still data to be used. <BR> <BR>Compare Ted Bundy. Almost all of his victims have a clear resemblence to one another, a few being very, very close in appearance. <BR> <BR>Another thing. Bundy usually targeted women who were 5&#39;00&#34;, to maybe 5&#39;03 in height. There&#39;s no question this was done so he could physically control the women, although thank heaven, one of them got away. <BR> <BR>Back to BTK. Does anyone know the height and approximate weight of the women who were his victims? Shirley Vian was a little heavyset &#40;so am I, I need to lose 35 pounds, so I&#39;m &#34;allowed&#34; to say that : &#41; and it would be interesting to know the height/weight of the women. Here&#39;s why: <BR> <BR>If one or more of them was, say, 5&#39;7&#34; or taller and seemed to have a decent amount of physical strength, it tells me that BTK was, during the attacks, fearless. True, BTK had a firearm and Bundy didn&#39;t, but BTK would still have probably known that a larger &#40;and by implication, stronger&#41; <BR>woman would be more likely to be able to wrest his gun from him than would a very petite woman.  <BR>This would also be a significant factor in profiling BTK. <BR> <BR>Vicky Wegerle. I can&#39;t make out her height and weight from the driver&#39;s license. Her weigt may say 115, but that&#39;s only a guess. Plus when you get your license, they don&#39;t take your height or weigh you. They write down what you tell them. <BR> <BR>Why did BTK choose her? Not because he liked a certain type &#40;in a physical sense&#41; of woman. Vicky was certainly stalked and the deranged mind <BR>of the sexual sadist BTK only knows for sure. <BR>Still, there are always clues and indicators. I really hope a geographic profiler is working on this case. I&#39;m beginning to think geography &#40;the location of the crime scenes, in combination with dates and classified data these profiler&#39;s use&#41; will play a key role in apprehending BTK. Finally, I notice that <BR>BTK drove Vicky&#39;s car a couple of blocks and abandoned it. He did the same with the Oteros. I&#39;d like to know why. My guess is that he drove the cars a couple blocks to his own vehicle, or perhaps a bus. To me, using a victim&#39;s car for two blocks is still bizarre behavior. <BR> <BR>Maybe BTK <b>walked</b> to his other crime scenes??? <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 594-->
<!--Post: 606--><!--Time: 1090900313-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST606"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, July 26, 2004 - 8:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Bookworm wrote: <BR> <BR><i>In Douglas&#39;s book Obsession he says BTK was complaining about the Otero&#39;s car being dirty. May be he liked cleanliness</i> <BR> <BR>This fits Mike Kelleher&#39;s profile, I think. If BTK <BR>had a job in a supervisory capacity, which I&#39;m beginning to believe more and more, the dirty car remark slides in flawlessly. By &#39;supervisory,&#39; I don&#39;t mean a bank president. It could be something simple, like &#34;Team Leader&#34; at McDonalds. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 606-->
<!--Post: 625--><!--Time: 1090966293-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST625"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Muskogee<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Muskogee<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, July 27, 2004 - 3:11 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George, height and weight don&#39;t necessarily have anything to do with physical ability &#40;in the sense of self-defense&#41;.  A 5&#39;00&#34; woman can beat the crap out of a 6&#39;5&#34; football player, if she knows how to use leverage properly.   <BR> <BR>Still, I think your point is quite valid because most women AREN&#39;T trained in self-defense.  This gives the person with brute strength &#40;usually the man&#41; the upper hand.  Additionally, a killer may still TARGET petite women because he ASSUMES they are not as able to fight back.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 625-->
<!--Post: 627--><!--Time: 1090972541-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST627"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, July 27, 2004 - 4:55 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi Muskogee, <BR> <BR>Thanks. In hindsight I do recall the post you made <BR>and the significance of leverage. I believe it was in Texas and you were a volunteer fire fighter&#40;?&#41; and said that there was only one guy there who could still best you in a fight; the rest of the men, I recall, you could have thrown around like rag dolls. <BR> <BR>I got caught up in &#34;Why Wegerle&#34; and forgot about your post. My bad.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
