<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST946"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, August 28, 2004 - 5:32 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Only 7% of serial killers attend church. BTK is always in the minority, thus befouling the typical profile. He has to be giving the impression of being a fine, upstanding, God fearing man to those around him. With paranoia increasing in Wichita, any perceived wierdness will be reported to the police. Only when the police release significant info about the killings can someone discover curiosities related to BTK and id him. <BR> <BR>And he has to have killed before the Oteros and has to have continued to do so over all these years unless he was physically restrained in some way or by some circumstances.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
