<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1204"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Quell<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Quell<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, October 13, 2004 - 7:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->P.J. Soles?  Do you think there is a coorelation between the &#34;shoes were together sir&#34; and P.J. Soles?  So that is the actress&#39;s name?  <BR> <BR>The guy is obviously as quirky as they come, but there is a definite stream of &#34;showman,&#34; possibly.  Because he is so camera oriented, this showmanship would go along with this &#34;visual&#34; thing.  His body image means alot to him?  Not that he is a model, but would have liked to become one?  Impossible type of career in his mind?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
