<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1209"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nostone<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nostone<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, October 14, 2004 - 10:02 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m sure I&#39;ve seen this posted elsewhere, but can&#39;t remember where...Wasn&#39;t the Ghostbusters program started after the last 70&#39;s murder and disbanded in late &#39;86?  Maybe they actually got too close to him and actually interviewed him or something.  When they disbanded GB, the coast was clear to murder, but not announce it for a while.  He maybe was having &#34;withdrawal&#34; so he killed Wegerle to get it out of his system. <BR> <BR>I&#39;m not positive this is so, he may have just continued killing all along.  It is kinda weird that he didn&#39;t contact for years though.  If he was killing, I&#39;m having a hard time imagining him not taunting all along.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
