<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1229"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, October 15, 2004 - 7:11 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Does anyone know if there were renovations to Vicki&#39;s church at the time of her death? Was there construction going on within &#39;sight&#39; of the church? Construction type activities might play some part ,as lots of people are involved, from direct hires to private contractors. Nancy Fox worked for a construction co. as well.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
