<!--Post: 7531--><!--Time: 1108563046-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7531"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 6:10 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Christa, Is there anyway you can go back and find out if any of the others victims went to your church? Maybe there kids went to Bible school, there would be a record at the church.  Bookworm can I get you to do something for us please? Go back to the murders, look at the list that Tom has at the beginning of the website the other&#39;s that may be linked, BTK&#39;s # is the # 3, most of the time, exclude the addresses of the victims who&#39;s house was set on fire and things that dont follow the pattern, of being strangled or stabbed. then map it, See the Ghostbusters didn&#39;t add the unsolved murders into the equation and I think If we do that it will give us a better Idea of where he is, I will research the unsolved murders and see If I can pick up the MO, Thanks. I believe Vickie knew the other victims somehow, lets figure out how.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7531-->
<!--Post: 9786--><!--Time: 1109638583-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9786"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jed4258<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jed4258<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 4:56 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It may just be speculation after the fact, but I have been struck with this,.. I read somewhere that Vicki was a active member of the St. Andrew Lutheran Church in Wichita, and we have learned that Denny the Dog Catcher was an active member of the Christ Lutheran Church listed as being in Augusta.  Could this be where he located her, using his position within the church to gain entry to the house?  I thought I had read that she was active in the Church&#39;s daycare.  I&#39;m sure revalation of this will come in the future.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9786-->
<!--Post: 11767--><!--Time: 1111150984-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11767"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 18, 2005 - 5:03 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Jed: It is highly probable that he was aware of her thru church affiliation. Though at different churches, they could have had shared functions, like a Thanksgiving Eve service, various committee work, parishioners knowing others from another congregation, etc. Perhaps there was a &#39;how can we improve nursery care&#39; get together, etc. That would be a vital topic for all churches who provide child care. I am sure that someone holds the key in knowledge somewhere. BTK was hyper-attuned to things that others would consider casual, so someone might deem their info not important. And after so many years, memories can fade and people die/move away. It must be remembered that he picked her. She did not set him off or entice him. He is the pervert.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11767-->
<!--Post: 12153--><!--Time: 1111675225-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12153"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 24, 2005 - 6:40 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Embersage, <BR>Sorry I&#39;ve been really busy and just had some time to scan some of the threads. Now we know who BTK is it could be easier to guess who could be the real BTK victims. <BR> <BR>The news showed a large round gold locket-like necklace that came in one of the BTK packages. Does anyone know if it was Vicky&#39;s?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12153-->
<!--Post: 12158--><!--Time: 1111678926-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12158"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsewhere<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsewhere<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 24, 2005 - 7:42 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have been asking that same question since DTDC arrest.  I haven&#39;t heard anything about who it belonged to.  All I know is that it was contained in the &#34;Fox News&#34; package...I have family in Wichita and they told me Fox released the contents to the public...I think it was the last drop BTK made...I am pretty sure.. <BR>I thought perhaps it belonged to &#34;Dee Davis&#34;...maybe that is one way they linked Denny Boy to her murder????????  Doesn&#39;t really look like a piece of jewelry a young woman would wear...but then again...I could be quite wrong.  P.S.  The package to Fox was also the one with the floppy in it that busted him.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12158-->
<!--Post: 12172--><!--Time: 1111702773-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12172"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 24, 2005 - 2:19 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have never heard who that locket belonged to but I have heard that of all the jewelery recovered in the canister at Dennis Rader&#39;s shed that none of it has been linked to the 10 victims he is charged with killing.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
